FLOW1
# f07: the TARGET-TEST path -> t02 params (falcon / tstage 1), plus the
# back edge and the addcode refusal:
#   - enter target-select, B back to menu-top (targetselect.js:76-81;
#     menuSelected stays TARGETTEST), A re-enter (the hand re-homes on
#     slot 0);
#   - ONE shoulder-L press wraps marth -> falcon (targetselect.js:62-66
#     — the wrap witness);
#   - the FREE HAND (DEVIATION D29, A25c) walks down the left column to
#     the addcode slot; A there is the registered refusal (builder
#     plane, foh.h); the hand walks back UP to slot 1 (tstage 1);
#   - A -> TLAUNCH char=4 tstage=1; the driver replays the frozen t02
#     trace through the launch seam (both streams judged).
#
# RE-CUT FOR D29 (A25c). The pre-D29 walk was five 3-frame DOWN taps and
# four 3-frame UP taps, because the cursor was an INDEX and one rising
# edge was one slot. The hand is LEVEL driven and moves FOH_CURSOR_VY =
# 3.84 px a frame, so the same journey is now two held runs. Nothing
# else moved: every event frame, every SHOT frame and every SHOT name is
# where it was, and flows/f07-target-t02.expect is BYTE-UNCHANGED.
#
# The two runs, measured against foh_tss_slots' rects (foh.h):
#   - the hand homes at slot 0's centre (58.0, 39.5);
#   - DOWN+RIGHT for 6 frames (401..406) -> (72.4, 62.54). The RIGHT is
#     not decoration: the addcode slot spans x 70..170 while the left
#     column spans x 8..108, so x = 58 would pass BELOW addcode and hit
#     nothing. 72.4 is inside both, which is why one run does both;
#   - DOWN for 22 more frames (407..428) -> (72.4, 147.02), inside
#     addcode's y 142..159. Crossing slots 1..4 on the way is what makes
#     this still the "walks 0 -> 4 -> addcode" gesture the old taps were;
#   - UP for 22 frames (438..459) -> back to (72.4, 62.54), slot 1.
I 1 -
I 375 S
I 376 -
I 380 D
I 383 -
I 385 A
I 386 -
I 390 B
I 391 -
I 395 A
I 396 -
I 400 K
I 401 DR
I 407 D
I 429 -
SHOT 430 tss-addcode
I 435 A
I 436 -
I 438 U
I 460 -
SHOT 460 tss-t02
I 465 A
I 466 -
END 470
